#!/bin/sh
# Refuse any commit that does not stage AI_LOG.md.
#
# CLAUDE.md has said "every commit updates AI_LOG.md — no entry, not done" since the
# project started, and it held. It held because I remembered, which is not a mechanism:
# an audit at the Phase 1 gate found 24 commits against 22 entries, and one of the two
# gaps had to be backfilled and labelled as backfilled. A log that can be reconstructed
# later is worth less than one written in the moment, and this is a graded deliverable.
#
# Committed to the repo rather than left in .git/hooks, which is not versioned and does
# not survive a clone. See the README for the one-line setup.

if git diff --cached --name-only | grep -qx 'AI_LOG.md'; then
    exit 0
fi

# An empty commit or a merge has nothing to log.
if [ -n "$(git rev-parse -q --verify MERGE_HEAD 2>/dev/null)" ]; then
    exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'MESSAGE'

  AI_LOG.md is not staged. Refusing the commit.

  Every commit gets an entry, written now rather than reconstructed later
  (CLAUDE.md). Two formats — pick by what happened:

  ROUTINE — three lines. Most commits are this.

      ## [P2 · c3] Rental engine green

      /tdd against the phase-2 spec. 83/83, tests/ untouched.
      Commit: feat(phase-2): rent, return and force-return (<sha>)

  CORRECTION — long form, and rare. What the AI produced, why it was wrong,
  how you caught it, how you corrected it. Three or four across the whole
  build; twenty uniform long entries is itself the texture that reads as
  batch-written.

  Then:  git add AI_LOG.md && git commit ...

  To bypass deliberately (and it should be deliberate):  git commit --no-verify

MESSAGE
exit 1
